{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1160953-wolf-s-rain-as-wtf-game","id":1160953,"title":"Wolf's Rain as WtF game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-20T13:25:49-08:00","id":1160953,"title":"Wolf's Rain as WtF game","content":"So <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter\">Story Letter</a> asked for this, but did not done himself. Let\u2019s look on one of interesting anime about wolves becoming humans ever created \u2013 as tale of <b>WtF</b> game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Let\u2019s talk <i>Wolf\u2019s Rain</i>!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://wolfsrain.wikia.com/wiki/Wolf%27s_Rain_Wiki\" target=\"_blank\">Source of information about series</a><br /> <br /> Beside <b>WtF</b> 2E corebook Bloods and Bones \u2013 I use some of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/432182-new-blood-and-bone-archetypes\">proposed by fans here</a>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wolf\u2019s Rain</b> setting:<ul><li>Story takes place in post-apocalyptic future where climate changed to next Ice Age. Humanity is on it\u2019s last grasps \u2013 end of human kind is possible if solution will not be found.</li> <li>In Uratha kind ( \u2018wolves\u2019 ) there is tale about Paradise that \u2013 when found \u2013 will fix a world. Connotation of recreating Pangea from WtF are obvious here.</li> <li>All Uratha are <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1122648-urhanu-%E2%80%93-wtf-wolf-based-werewolves\">Urhanu</a> \u2013 they are all born as wolves become humans for survival, not the other way around.</li> <li>Uratha can only take Hishu and Urhan forms.</li> <li>There are no direct Tribes, but story of Paradise seems to point in previous times Tribes culture could existed. I pointed to Tribes characters would have if those factions existed in series.</li> </ul>Main characters:<ul><li><b>Kiba</b> \u2013 Blood: Alpha, Bone: Lone Wolf, Auspice: Elodoth, Tribe: Storm Lords</li> <li><b>Tsume </b>\u2013 Blood: Monster, Bone: Wallflower, Auspice: Rahu, Tribe: Iron Masters</li> <li><b>Hige </b>\u2013 Blood: Fox, Bone: Hedonist, Auspice: Cahalith, Tribe: Hunter in Darkness</li> <li><b>Toboe </b>\u2013 Blood: Omega, Bone: Cub, Auspice: Irraka, Tribe: None? He does not seem to choose any philosophy in series.</li> <li><b>Blue </b>\u2013 Blood: Beta, Bone: Role Model, Auspice: Rahu</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-26-2017, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T03:16:14-08:00","id":1161117,"title":"","content":"hahahahaha you are unbeliavable <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T10:21:45-08:00","id":1161195,"title":"","content":"Would Cheza be a promethean made of wolf blood and lunar energy?<br /> <br /> While the actual tribes don't exist, most of the wolves might fit the 1e tribes (ie no sacred prey, more personality wise) if they are taken less as a social group and more a line of descent and archetype. Like Kiba as a storm lord, Hige and Toboe are Iron Masters, Tsume is a Hunter in Darkness (Or maybe storm Lord or bone shadow) and Blue is a ghost wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T11:45:39-08:00","id":1161225,"title":"","content":"No, she is manifested pagaean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 12-24-2017, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T11:54:32-08:00","id":1161232,"title":"","content":"Why not have both! Perhaps she is a Promethean made from Lunar power to evolve into a qasmal whose mission is to bring back Pangaea and evolve into a Pangaean. Its.. entirely strange, certainly, but... It would work. Granted, it relies on the small but iirc wyrd supported idea that some promethean choose a pilgrimage to become something other than human, but for this storyline, it seems to fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T06:45:07-08:00","id":1161499,"title":"","content":"No this is a WtF core setting, only core WtF stuff allowed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T04:42:03-08:00","id":1170139,"title":"","content":"I added Tribes to characters I think more work with TV series as I re-watch it. Kiba is proud Storm Lord that has 'vision of Paradise' and fighting with weaknesses in wolf kind. Tsume is clearly examplar Iron Master, using humans to his own ends. Hige is much more 'I live in city and get food from humans' Iron Master. And Toboe does not seem to choose Tribe stance yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T05:50:08-08:00","id":1170154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1160953-wolf-s-rain-as-wtf-game?p=1170139#post1170139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I added Tribes to characters I think more work with TV series as I re-watch it. Kiba is proud Storm Lord that has 'vision of Paradise' and fighting with weaknesses in wolf kind. Tsume is clearly examplar Iron Master, using humans to his own ends. Hige is much more 'I live in city and get food from humans' Iron Master. And Toboe does not seem to choose Tribe stance yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What do you think Toboe chooses for a Trbe after they defeated the huge walrus? They did fight awesomely like a pack back then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T06:13:04-08:00","id":1170158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1160953-wolf-s-rain-as-wtf-game?p=1170154#post1170154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think Toboe chooses for a Trbe after they defeated the huge walrus? They did fight awesomely like a pack back then.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will answer it when I see walrus. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm just now after war machine episode and past 'City of Dogs' episodes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T07:48:14-08:00","id":1170173,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Coolness <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> sorry for spoiler <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T13:33:25-08:00","id":1170521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1160953-wolf-s-rain-as-wtf-game?p=1161195#post1161195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Cheza be a promethean made of wolf blood and lunar energy?</div> </div> </div> </div>As seeing now first episode where <b>Cheza</b> is awake ( and fallen from the sky ) I think, as she is Moon Flower Maiden - that she is <i><u>Luna's Herald,</u></i> locked into artificial body! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Think about it - IF we treat Luna as she was able to do stuff like Idigam ( that in <b>WtF</b> she clearly can, there are even rumors Idigam ARE Luna's Children, in the end ) - And one of Idigam powers is Forge Herald - And Moon Flower is indication of Mother Moon influence on the world in <b>Wolf's Rain</b> - It kinda makes sense that <i>Cheza</i>, Maiden made of Moon Flower, will be Herald for the Luna herself. Artificially created by humans, but Herald of Moon non the less! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Maybe Luna choose her as proper Herald when she awoken - and before she just smelled a lot of Moon Flowers, so Kiba followed her smell, 'instinctively'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-25-2017, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T22:18:48-08:00","id":1170606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1160953-wolf-s-rain-as-wtf-game?p=1170139#post1170139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hige is much more 'I live in city and get food from humans' Iron Master.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seen now 10 episodes - I'm after Forest of Dead in storyline - Hige looks to me as much more Hunter in Darkness. He survives anything and anywhere, always giving Toboe remarks that cub cannot take care for himself or not understanding ecosystem. Hige is just much more 'city dwelling' HiD as it's easier for him to live there, but get's fine once they are in the wild, on pilgrimage to Paradise. Still, he seems to not understand humans so much as Tsume, so this is why second one is Iron Master more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-26-2017, 01:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T06:17:25-08:00","id":1170660,"title":"","content":"Tsume and Kiba are both Rahu aspects, Kiba a stormlord and Tsume a Blood Talon.<br /> Hige suits more for iron master for his human affinity.<br /> Toboe might be more suited for Hunter after some pack tactics and successful hunting, he may have experience with humans but he hides surprises. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T10:43:43-08:00","id":1170724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1160953-wolf-s-rain-as-wtf-game?p=1170660#post1170660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tsume and Kiba are both Rahu aspects, Kiba a stormlord and Tsume a Blood Talon.<br /> Hige suits more for iron master for his human affinity.<br /> Toboe might be more suited for Hunter after some pack tactics and successful hunting, he may have experience with humans but he hides surprises. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I will let you disagree pacifistically, as I have readings much more stronger with each rewatched episode and I stay with my associations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T00:51:39-08:00","id":1170875,"title":"","content":"So my players are arguing with me about my interpretation of anime, so I can as well sum up here my Auspice and Tribe association for each wolf - and reasons behind them.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Kiba</i></b><b>:</b><ul><li><b>Elodoth</b> \u2013 Rahu want\u2019s to solve conflicts and his own victory, often solving things alone. Kiba, instead, is making many decisions because they are \u2018honorable\u2019. He almost constantly goes to CONVINCE others to his actions and so the follow him. Compare his actions with Tsume in anime. What\u2019s more, in 2E Elodoths can soother but also to CALL a Death Rage in other Uratha \u2013 see how actions of Kiba works on others. He is clearly much more Elodoth, than Rahu.</li> <li><b>Storm Lords</b> \u2013 Kiba does not recognize any Weakness, in himself or in other wolves, even more he wants to lead the pack. It\u2019s perfect fulling of Lords Ban: \u201cAllow No One to Witness or to Tend Your Weakness.\u201d</li> </ul><b><i>Tsume</i></b><b>:</b><ul><li><b>Rahu</b> \u2013 Tsume sees everything as conflict that needs to be solved and is first to use violence. He is also the most \u2018tactical\u2019 of wolves.</li> <li><b>Iron Masters </b>\u2013 Few times in anime is called that Tsume feels best in city and best understand humans - even if he despises them.</li> </ul><b><i>Hige:</i></b><ul><li><b>Cahalith </b>\u2013 Hige is \u2018older brother\u2019 for the rest of pack, saying \u2018we must end arguing and do this\u2019 ( most mostly agreeing with Kiba plans ). It\u2019s a bit more interpretation from 1E, but Cahalith is \u2018support\u2019 in pack, solving tensions inside it. Elodoth convince other to his reasons - Cahalith want everyone to cooperate with each other ( and has Gifts for this ).</li> <li><b>Hunters in Darkness</b> \u2013 most often Hige reprimands Toboe that he does not understand life and not handle his hunts or taking care of food. He starts it in city, but in wilds continues those chiding the cub.</li> </ul><b><i>Toboe:</i></b><ul><li><b>Irraka</b> \u2013 Toboe is most withdrawn wolf during the action. Many times he is shown that he loves to sneak up on others.</li> <li>I\u2019m now in half of episodes and I still do not see Toboe to choose the way of thinking of anyone Tribe.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-27-2017, 03:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T10:00:21-08:00","id":1170976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1160953-wolf-s-rain-as-wtf-game?p=1170875#post1170875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my players are arguing with me about my interpretation of anime, so I can as well sum up here my Auspice and Tribe association for each wolf - and reasons behind them.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's your players opinion on this topic ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T10:42:57-08:00","id":1170992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1160953-wolf-s-rain-as-wtf-game?p=1170976#post1170976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's your players opinion on this topic ?</div> </div> </div> </div>They seems to agree on my reasoning as shown in my previous post now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T03:54:38-08:00","id":1171761,"title":"","content":"I just ended the TV series. It's ending is... interesting.<br /> <br /> But returning to Toboe question - After Walrus battle, I would marking him becoming Blood Talon - from the Ban of \u201cOffer No Surrender You Would Not Accept.\u201d - However just after this plot is ending, threads are closed and end game is on, so wolf character returns to their main characteristics - and Toboe just returns to his default 'obvious cub' archetype. In the end - Toboe does not go over with choosing proper Blood Talons, in point of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T06:25:50-08:00","id":1171776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1160953-wolf-s-rain-as-wtf-game?p=1171761#post1171761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just ended the TV series. It's ending is... interesting.<br /> <br /> But returning to Toboe question - After Walrus battle, I would marking him becoming Blood Talon - from the Ban of \u201cOffer No Surrender You Would Not Accept.\u201d - However just after this plot is ending, threads are closed and end game is on, so wolf character returns to their main characteristics - and Toboe just returns to his default 'obvious cub' archetype. In the end - Toboe does not go over with choosing proper Blood Talons, in point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Toboe is a wonderful example of a possible, even unique past lives merit. The changes on his character before and after the ''world resurrection'' are unique.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T06:26:50-08:00","id":1171777,"title":"","content":"IMHO the series is a great inspiration for werewolf characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T07:47:10-08:00","id":1171787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1160953-wolf-s-rain-as-wtf-game?p=1171776#post1171776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Toboe is a wonderful example of a possible, even unique past lives merit. The changes on his character before and after the ''world resurrection'' are unique.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there second season or movie of Wolf's Rain I did not know about? <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Last scene of 30th episodes is showing the wolf pack living now second lives in our modern city. I do not see any character changes in 'world resurrection' as there is literally just one his short showing for few seconds in frame at end of this episode. </div></div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> I also cannot find <i>Past Lives</i> Merit in <b>WtF</b> 2E corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T10:45:30-08:00","id":1171829,"title":"","content":"No I am afraid there is no other season or a movie.<br /> <br /> The Past Lives Merit is not in WtF 2E, its a <b>Merit</b> from Werewolf Transation guide Book called <b>Ancestors</b>, in <b>page 35</b>.<br /> <br /> Once per session you can call ancestral memories and increase your skill dots depending on how many dots you have on this merit.<br /> The effect lasts for an entire scene.<br /> In the case of Toboe the ancestor is himself.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T00:55:05-08:00","id":1171969,"title":"","content":"Thats a great use of Weather and strength gifts (aka Rahu Storm Lord)<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=diaqpvV4yAQ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg